I just came to the conclusion that many of my short-lived games are
indirectly due to risky attempts at gaining poison resistance. That's to
say, I find I need to get PR before say Dlvl 6, when orc gangs start
appearing. So I take a gamble on eating poisonous critters, hoping
to get the "healthy" message, but usually before then I've ruined my
character by sapping her strength and what not.

So what's a good strategy to acquiring PR? And don't say tinning or
amulet, I'm talking short games here, before I've seen (or IDed) such
things.

Which also makes me think: other intrinsics come comparatively easily,
at least with no concomitant risk. Unfair, no? Sure, eating a winter
wolf should give you a chance to acquire CR, but there should be also
some probability of instead catching the Big Chill.

